Purpose
If the screen width is less than 600 pixels, display a ListView (mobile layout).
If the screen width is 600 pixels or more, display a GridView (tablet/desktop layout).
Step 1: Import Material Package
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';
Explanation

This imports Flutter's Material Design library, which contains widgets like:

MaterialApp
Scaffold
AppBar
Card
ListView
GridView
Icon
Text

Without this import, these widgets cannot be used.

Step 2: main() Function
void main() {
  runApp(const MyApp());
}
Explanation

Every Flutter application starts execution from the main() function.

runApp() launches the Flutter application.

main()
   │
   ▼
runApp(MyApp)
Step 3: MyApp Class
class MyApp extends StatelessWidget {
Explanation

MyApp is the root widget of the application.

It extends StatelessWidget, meaning:

It has no mutable state.
Its UI only changes when Flutter rebuilds it due to external changes.
Step 4: Constructor
const MyApp({super.key});
Explanation
const creates an immutable widget, improving performance.
super.key passes the widget key to the parent class, helping Flutter efficiently identify widgets during rebuilds.
Step 5: build() Method
@override
Widget build(BuildContext context)
Explanation

Every widget must implement a build() method.

It returns the widget tree that Flutter displays on the screen.

Step 6: MaterialApp
return MaterialApp(
Explanation

MaterialApp is the root widget for a Material Design application.

It provides:

Themes
Navigation
Routing
Material styling
Step 7: Remove Debug Banner
debugShowCheckedModeBanner: false,

Removes the red DEBUG banner that appears in debug mode.

Step 8: Home Screen
home: const ResponsiveUI(),

This tells Flutter that ResponsiveUI is the first screen shown when the app starts.

Step 9: ResponsiveUI Class
class ResponsiveUI extends StatelessWidget {

This widget decides which layout to display based on the screen width.

Step 10: Get Screen Width
double screenWidth = MediaQuery.of(context).size.width;
Explanation

MediaQuery provides information about the current device.

Examples:

Property	Meaning
size.width	Screen width
size.height	Screen height
orientation	Portrait or landscape

Example values:

Mobile → 390
Tablet → 800
Desktop → 1366
